In accordance to the Sendai Disaster Reduction Framework 2015-2030, this priority area promote S&T initiatives for the substantial reduction of disaster risk and losses in lives, livelihoods and health in the economic, physical, social, cultural and environmental assets of persons, businesses, communities and countries; and promotes investments in disaster risk reduction for resilience by stimulating and contributing to developing of the knowledge, capacities and motivation for disaster risk reduction at all levels.

Disaster Risk Reduction and Climate Change Adaptation is very significant in inclusive and sustainable development. Hence, the S&T activities and innovation in these areas are prioritized by the Philippine Government as harmonized by the Department of Science and Technology. In the health sector, several gaps have been identified in these areas:
1. Identification of top climate related diseases which causes morbidities and mortalities;
2. Food security and nutrition during disasters in the health perspective;
3. S&T based innovations in building resilient health systems during disasters

The core aim of the Relief Assistance Program is to deliver immediate and effective help to people in crisis situations, such as natural and human-induced calamities. Specifically, this program aims to:

1. To create a disaster-resilient Muslim community;
2. To empower the Muslim community through knowledge and capacity development on climate change action, mitigation, and adaptation;
3. To provide the underserved Muslim Filipinos, a NCMF relief box that is culturally sensitive-appropriate to their needs; and
4. To deliver timely to underserved Muslim Filipinos an NCMF Relief Box containing halal-certified goods, sajadah, hijab, and basic necessities and toiletries during emergencies.

PROJECT ANDAM of the DILG VIII is designed to strengthen the disaster preparedness and resilience of communities across Eastern Visayas. To be implemented initially in ten (10) barangays as the pilot LGUs, the project supports the PDP and EV RDP thrusts of enhancing public awareness and readiness in the face of natural hazards.

Anchored on the principles of proactive disaster risk reduction, PROJECT ANDAM aims to equip households and barangays with clear, accessible, and actionable information on the hazards affecting their area. Through intensified public education, customized hazard signage, community-level preparedness measures, and improved communication protocols, the project seeks to empower families to make informed decisions before, during, and after disasters.

Aligned with the strategies outlined in the Disaster Preparedness Manual of Operation Listo, PROJECT ANDAM reinforces early warning, preparedness, and response mechanisms essential in mitigating potential impacts—such as loss of lives, injuries, and damage to property. By fostering quick response actions and strengthening household-level awareness, the project contributes to building a culture of preparedness within the region.

The project involves the implementation of capacity-building and systems-strengthening activities in cities/municipalities in the region, including:
•        Capacity development training for LGUs and Local DRRM Councils on DRRM planning and emergency operations;
•        Simulation exercises and contingency planning workshops to test and refine preparedness and response mechanisms;
•        Technical assistance for the formulation, updating, and harmonization of Local DRRM Plans (LDRRMPs) and Local Climate Change Action Plans (LCCAPs);
•        Documentation and sharing of best practices, serving as a platform for learning and replication; and
•        Support for the DILG’s Operation L!STO campaign, reinforcing a culture of readiness before, during, and after disasters.
